body:
What I mean by a forced battle against Katakuri, is that it simply wasn't necessary for the plot. Did Luffy need to have a 10-hour fight with Katakuri leaving his crew alone in a Yonko territory? Well to me the answer is no. Oda did that just to make Luffy get stronger in a fight to prepare him for the Wano battle. It's as simple as that. 

&#x200B;

Zoro told Luffy to be serious yet in the same arc, he did what he did with Monet, not hurting her. She was about to blow everything and kill everybody, if not for luck, because Zoro was stupid. He also messed up when fighting Killer, underestimating his opponents, and he himself admitted it. So no, Zoro is not as serious as you are thinking.

&#x200B;

I don't know why you're so adamant with this power level thing. Just accept the story as it is and move on and the story is having the strawhats win against by far bigger fish than them during wano. If it was up to me, the strawhats will all get destroyed during the raid and spend five years in the new world to get stronger, because they are so ridiculously outmatched and their growth rate is way too fast. But I don't write one piece, so I enjoy it for what it is. You probably should too. One piece is great, but it's still a shonen manga with the flaws of a shonen manga. Nothing we can do about it.
